# Freestanding host-test build output. Everything here is regenerated by run.py on
# every invocation (including the link inputs in host-link/), so none of it belongs
# in version control: *.obj/*.exe are per-run, and the .lib files are synthesised
# from the .def files next to them.
*.obj
*.exe
*.pdb
*.lib

# Transaction snapshots. These describe one specific change against one specific
# baseline commit and are refreshed in place; git already holds both endpoints, so
# keeping a second copy of the same bytes only lets the two drift apart.
MODIFIED_FILE.zip
ORIGINAL_FILE.zip
PRE_PULL_SOURCE.zip
DIFF_FILE.patch
*hashes.json

# Evidence dumps: screen captures, screen recordings, logcat pulls, APK copies.
*.png
*.mp4
*.log
*.apk
*.jsonl
*.measurement.json
*-track.json
*measurement.json
commands.jsonl
device-commands.jsonl

# One-shot run leftovers: a gradle exit code, an install log naming the APK it
# happened to install, single-recording frame measurements, a pre-pull manifest,
# and the device prefs snapshots taken around a restart. Each described one run
# on one machine and says nothing a rerun would not.
build-result.txt
*-install.txt
*-device.txt
*-measure.txt
pull-result.txt
pre-pull-manifest.json
restart.txt
*settings*.json

# Trees materialised by run.py baseline/rollback to build the "before" sources.
baseline-tree/
rollback-tree/
pull-merge/
